WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
<b>Drawing Fun!</b>

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.200
Drawing

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.580
F - U - N !

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.960
Big Sister Kisaragi, Big Sister Kisaragi!

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.410
What's the matter, Suneko-san?

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.120
Did you know that today

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.990
we have a guest!

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.510
Thanks. I'm Tomokane.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.220
Wow! How wonderful!

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.610
That's right. 
I've done just about everything.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.380
Like climb a tree and have the 
branch break underneath...

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.850
She's just talking about whatever she wants, right?

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:21.860
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.540
I really liked those “working cars” 
when I was a kid.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.050
Really?

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.750
I used to have cardboard 
cars made for me

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.940
and I'd pretend to 
drive around in them.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.000
I wonder what happened to those?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.170
I have no idea.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.260
And so...

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.510
They were really sturdy, you know?

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.960
GA Geijutsuka Art Design Class...

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.490
is about to start!

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.120
Oh?

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:56.500
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.080
<b>Blood Drive</b>

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.710
Huh?

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:17.580
That's the...

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.650
It's the bloodmobile.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.090
Oh! So it really is!

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.590
This is the first time 
I've seen one up close!

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.200
Buchi-san, look!

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.650
That's the car they 
collect blood in, right?!

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.600
It's rude to point, Aa-san.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:34.070
Hmm? So, this is what the principal's 
new car looks like this time.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:38.030
Maybe once you turn 74 you go for 
these instead of imported cars.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.610
Sorry. I have no idea how 
to even respond to that.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.610
<b>The Border Between Life and Death</b>

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.610
Help Out the Blood Drive of Love!NAt the School Gates, In Front of University Building 1
Dates and Times

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.810
Oh. So the bloodmobile is here today.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.310
Good morning.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.980
They came here often when 
I was a student, too!

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.030
Oh, Usami-sensei, you're 
a graduate from here?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:04.550
But I've never once donated blood,

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.480
even though I'm kind of interested...

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.680
Why don't you?

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.530
They said they were running low.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.800
Let's see. Cigarettes, cigarettes.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.600
Sasamoto-sensei!

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:14.340
<b>Rip</b>

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.870
Won't you come with me?

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.200
What are you, a schoolgirl who 
can't go to the bathroom alone?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.980
But I feel uneasy. 
I don't think I can go alone!

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.580
Then, why don't you ask Sotoma-sensei?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.990
He's in charge, you should be relying on him.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.750
That doesn't really matter, does it?

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.490
Staff Room

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:32.990
You're annoying!

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.860
Meanie!

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.730
Oh, c'mon.
 Hey, Sotoma-sensei.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.900
Can you take her to the blood drive?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:41.630
Blood drive?

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.510
Oh, perfect.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.640
I was just about to ask you about it!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:04:00.050
<b>GA1 Homeroom Teacher   Assistant Homeroom Teacher</b>

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.250
Since everybody is being asked to donate blood,

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.940
including the high school students,

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.590
if there are any volunteers, 
could you take them with you?

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:57.280
Oh, I see. That.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.350
Of course.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.650
So, at some point today,

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.590
there may be an announcement 
calling for blood donations.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.890
And...

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.560
They're also holding a contest 
for a blood donation mascot.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:16.010
We'll be working on this in our 
5th and 6th period design class.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.200
Make sure you read it over.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.600
Sotoma-sensei!

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.900
In other words, when you got to donate blood,

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.510
you're allowed to skip class, right?

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.850
You'll ask anything without 
hesitation, won't you?

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:28.730
Well, anyway...
 Yes, that's right.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.280
Pick whenever you prefer.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.090
Once you turn 16, of course.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.290
Whaaat?!

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.290
You may donate blood if you are 16 or older.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.970
The teacher saw right through us.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.760
So is Namiko-san the only one 
here who can donate blood?

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.720
Are you going to, Namiko-dono?

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.930
To be honest I could've 
gone either way,

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.250
but seeing Noda like 
this I suddenly want to!

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.770
Damn you, Namiko-san.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:53.780
Aww! I wanted to see what
 the inside of that van looked like!

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:57.170
<b>Under 16 
 Confidential!</b>

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.180
I don't really have any idea 
what goes on in a blood draw, either.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.000
Me neither.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.030
When I was in elementary school,

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.120
I didn't even know what the
"blood drive" in "blood drive van" was.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:08.190
I thought they were cars 
that ran on blood for fuel!

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.480
I'd wonder which blood 
type was the fastest...

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.100
That's...

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.490
Good for the earth...

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.080
But bad for people.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.490
How much blood would you need?

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.460
Staff Room

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.370
Searching for a blood drive mascot?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.870
<b>GA3  Homeroom Teacher</b>

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.870
Yeah. Could you post 
those around school?

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.310
What does a blood drive 
need a mascot for?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.190
There are many uses,

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.380
like for commercials or for flyers.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.000
Also, you've seen these 
things around, right?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:36.150
Please Donate to the Blood Drive!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.150
Oh! Mascot costumes!

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.870
That's one of the things I 
want to do when I grow up!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.830
And have children grab me!

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.730
Then my dream is to receive a

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.920
packet of tissues from 
Aa-san when I grow up.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.010
Sounds fun, right?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.900
Ah, youth is bright with so many useless dreams.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.060
I went to the blood drive's website

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.410
and collected things 
that might help us out.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:06.500
Oh, good work, Kyouju.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.910
Hmm, there sure are a lot of different 
images for each prefecture.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.360
I guess the fact that most of them use 
a heart motif is because, you know,

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.420
it means like “love and peace," right?

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:17.220
They do call it the
 “blood drive of love."

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.890
Really? It isn't because 
blood comes from the heart?

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:23.900
Of course...

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.390
Her face is red.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.670
Although, it's not like
you're completely wrong.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:29.880
She's probably thinking to herself,

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.170
“I just said something 
completely out of character."

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.940
Then to have Kisaragi-chan 
say that to her...

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.080
Excuse me.

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:41.150
Could I please have all 
blood drive volunteers?

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.470
Right. I'm off!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.580
Be quiet on your way out.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.710
I feel kind of nervous.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.000
Actually, I am too!

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.170
Oh? Usami-sensei, are you 
going to do it, as well?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.220
Oh, actually, I was debating 
it up until just now.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.360
But since my students are doing it,

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.710
I figured I should be brave, as well.

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:02.600
Then, we'll expect you
 to set a good example!

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:03.600
Umm...

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:08.120
but maybe after I make sure 
that you all are okay first...

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:08.870
Right?

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.890
I mean, it's my responsibility.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:11.820
That's weird.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.380
I can't seem to see that bravery 
you were talking about.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.650
<b>Please Donate Blood</b>

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.650
Red Blood Cell–kun

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.650
There are lots of different mascots, aren't there?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.920
But none of them really stand out...

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:29.430
<b>Please Donate Blood</b>

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.080
Heh, this character's pretty funny.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.440
Oh, I get it.
A vampire.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.070
Then what about mosquitos or leeches?

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:29.290
It's original!

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.780
But that's kind of hard 
to like, isn't it?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.700
The whole blood-sucking image.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.640
After all, since the character 
is being used for PR,

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.310
it should attract interest.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:40.040
In that case,

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.250
shouldn't it be a character that

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.040
makes you want to give blood 
by looking at it?

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.000
Hmm! In other words, 
something like this!

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.040
<b>Please Donate Blood</b>

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.250
All the drawings end up looking 
sort of the same, don't they?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.110
I guess what you imagine when you think of donating blood

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.010
is pretty well defined.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.070
So, of course, they'll look the same.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.240
Then, why don't we take 
turns and say whatever

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.820
comes to mind when we think 
of “blood donation”?

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.770
Counterclockwise, okay?

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.240
Yes, let's.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.020
Okay!

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:17.840
Ready and...

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:19.840
Scene of an accident!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.150
Blood transfusion.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:24.220
Blood red!

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:25.620
Rose.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:27.530
A Love Hate Drama

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.420
L-like love affairs?

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.360
The pressuring husband, 
the fleeing wife!

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:34.390
Extramarital investigation.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:36.660
Photographic evidence of the crime.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.630
Um... um... d-domestic fight!

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:43.700
The overcome husband confronts 
the wife's partner...

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.600
Overcome with anger: a bloodbath.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.240
The sound of sirens in the distance.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:51.300
Next, Namiko-san!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.010
W-wha? Scene of an accident.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.030
Correct!

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.530
Wow!

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.320
Welcome back.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.020
How did it go?

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.340
Well... pretty much what I expected.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.410
I felt a little weak 
afterwards, though.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.680
Hey, hey!

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:06.290
What do you do?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.450
Let's see.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:10.020
First they checked my blood 
pressure and did a blood test.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.980
Then they had me lie 
down and drew blood.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:13.830
I guess.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:17.390
The feeling of the needle 
stuck inside was a little...

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.300
Oh, and they gave me juice.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.580
Was there anyone who 
cried from the pain?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.950
We're not little kids.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:28.810
Ahh... well, no one cried 
during the blood draw...

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:36.590
<b>Sob sob</b>

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.260
What happened to Usami-sensei?

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.020
Apparently, she didn't weigh 
enough to donate blood

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.590
and was turned away at the door.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.670
In the end, because of the time it took

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.440
to donate blood, I didn't get to draw a mascot.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:46.570
And I wanted to donate blood instead.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:50.370
It looks like there's 
still time before the deadline.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.400
It's already gone.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:55.010
<b>Gone</b>

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.400
When we saw it this morning, 
it was parked right here, right?

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:57.950
It's still warm!

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.230
It hasn't gotten far.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:01.270
As if!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.420
<b>One Month Later</b>

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.920
By the way, about the blood 
drive mascot search,

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:11.290
it looks like one of the students 
in your class got an award, right?

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:12.320
What?

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.930
Did we have a contest like that?

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:18.300
Hold on. So that means she doesn't 
even know about it yet?

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.430
Please go let her know right away.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.930
Mascot Contest
Award Winning Pieces
Ayanoi Academy    3rd Year     Awara Chikako

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:24.690
Ayanoi Academy, 3rd year,
 Awara Chikako.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:27.970
Oh, there she is.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.490
Hey, Awara.

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:31.910
About the blood drive mascot thing,

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.440
looks like you won an award.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:34.620
What?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.700
Did I submit something 
to a contest like that?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.420
It must've been that one.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:39.860
You were saying how nice

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.600
it would be to hand out tissues 
in a costume like this,

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.720
and doodling something.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.030
Maybe I did draw something...

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:47.070
You don't even remember 
if you did or not!

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.500
Like teacher, like student...

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.700
Excuse me.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.720
Um, is Morita-sensei here?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:58.500
Oh, it looks like he's 
not here at the moment.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.500
<b> Morita-sensei's Desk</b>

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.700
Is that so?

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:00.510
In that case,

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.680
could you let him know that 
Tomokane went home early?

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.990
I have the nurse's 
permission as well, so...

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:08.830
Oh, okay.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.790
Well then. Excuse me.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.840
So he's named Tomokane, too.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:23.660
Completely different from the 
Tomokane in my class, though.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.730
Quiet and polite attitude.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.980
If you could add them together and 
divide by two they'd be just right.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:31.300
Oh, Morita-sensei!

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:32.320
Yes?

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:35.310
A student from your class, 
Tomokane-kun, went home early.

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.780
I see.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.870
Sasamoto-sensei.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:39.980
Is this the right one?

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.210
Oh, thanks!

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:42.780
You could've bought the 
whole carton, though.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.650
Please limit yourself.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:47.440
You've been doing more smoking recently.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:50.590
Hey. Tono-sensei got scolded.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:51.490
Shut it.

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:54.020
You too, Sotoma-sensei.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.280
Drinking too much coffee 
is bad for your stomach.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.650
Let's see... Water...

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:06.540
By the way, Usami-sensei, 
what are those?

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:08.390
Supplements!

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.330
But, are you supposed

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.880
to take as many supplements 
as you are years old?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.050
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:22.050
Geijutsuka Art Design Class

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.000
Oh, Morita-sensei!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.070
Yes?

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:28.780
Man, why are Mondays so depressing?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.030
Another week of school, huh?

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:32.000
Now, now.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.340
They say that when you sigh 
your happiness escapes.

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:36.650
We're still young, right?

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.000
You talk like the lady down the street.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:40.400
<b>Clap</b>

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:41.210
Ha!

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.670
I just caught some of that happiness!

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.710
You! Smashing people's 
happiness like a mosquito.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.310
That's your objection?!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.650
In other words, Namiko-san,

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:54.430
it's because you 
think of the repetition

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:57.280
of Monday through Friday 
that you become depressed.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.820
What? So you were listening.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.330
Then it's simple.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:03.340
Simply add a little 
spice to your everyday.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.600
Put some variety in your life.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.600
<b>Var  iety</b>

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.450
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.310
Whenever this princess 
acts like this...

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:12.710
To begin with, why don't you try 
something that you don't normally do?

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:15.570
Take it again from when you 
entered the classroom.

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:17.090
Should we go back together?

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.730
Something I don't usually do...

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.670
The assignment is “The border 
between life and death."

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.110
There's an assignment?

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.360
Hey!

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.120
Good morning.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.500
Good morning!

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.620
Huh? Are you the only one here, Noda?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:28.950
<b>Crash bang thump</b>

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:29.990
Whoa! What's going on?!

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:33.090
I've been hit.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:34.720
I won't make it.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:38.000
The enemy attack has 
annihilated first company, Sir!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.000
What?!

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:46.110
Please... tell my girl back home...
 that I love her...

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:48.060
Stay with me, Private John!

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:48.730
John?

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:52.020
Medic! Medic! Where's the medic?!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.930
You're lively today, as well.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.650
I guess there's nothing about Monday 
mornings that depresses them.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:00.550
Hot!

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.350
What?

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.600
I just added a little 
too much boiling water.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.370
I might've burned myself a little.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.360
Then you'd better run it 
under cold water right away.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.500
Let me see.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:09.960
Let's see here.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.110
Oh! It's hot!

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:13.610
Oh! It's hot!

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.170
Oh, no. I'm not 
participating in this.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:17.530
Oh! Cold!

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.740
Let's go to the nurse's office.

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:26.880
How are you going to pick all these up?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.220
I'll take care of it.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:31.810
Wh-whoa that's awesome.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:32.920
Is that a magnet?

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:36.390
Ooh! Kyouju! Let me do it, too! 
Let me do it!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.220
Wha? Whaaa?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.410
Wait, don't tell me 
that the magnet was...

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.580
Is your hand all right now?

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.900
Yes! They applied some salve.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:53.150
Now then, today's 
lunch is Tsukimi-Udon!

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.410
Same here!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:57.720
What's wrong, Noda-chan?!

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:59.060
Are you feeling unwell?

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.860
Calm down, Kisaragi.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:03.510
Not really. But right now...

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:04.650
Princess!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.420
Princess, I have returned from the

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.420
East building vending machine 
with the cure-all elixir!

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.680
Thank you, Lord Belmont.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.090
But, alas, I am already...

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:16.080
Princess!!

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.930
So you were doing that again!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:21.930
Lord Belmont, the only solution is 
to feed it to her mouth to mouth.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.370
Spit it out at the last second!

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:23.830
<b> Chirp!</b>

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:25.980
I'm all better!
 I'm absolutely all better!

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.750
She's back.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.700
Is that takikomi gohan?

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:34.870
Mmm, nope. It's only got bamboo 
shoots, so it's bamboo gohan.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.030
Takikomi-gohan's got all kinds 
of different ingredients, right?

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:39.680
That's not necessarily true...

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.030
Isn't it called takikomi gohan 
because something's been mixed in?

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.030
Takikomu = Mix In

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:46.590
Then, would you call sekihan 
 takikomi gohan, as well?

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:46.590
Sekihan = Red Rice

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.930
And kuri gohan, too?

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.930
Kuri = Chestnut Rice

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.930
T-Those are...!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.040
Classes of takikomi gohan!

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:52.820
Classes?

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:53.420
<b> Types</b>

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.070
Okay everyone, attention.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.000
Muffins for desert!

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.070
They're chocolate banana.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.520
Huh? What? Did you make these?

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.680
Yup! Want one?

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:06.430
W-when did you pick up 
such a girly technique?!

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.430
Even though you're Noda...

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:08.890
Well, as long as it's 
something like this,

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.250
I make these once in a while.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.710
You Mafia girl!

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:12.560
Mafia?

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.530
Those who eat muffins are all Mafia!

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.590
Is that true?!

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:17.480
Wow.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:19.720
I'm impressed by people who 
can make stuff like this easily.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:22.180
Namiko-san, you can't cook?

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:24.630
Well, it's not like I can't cook,

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.570
but I'm a little more 
artistic than most people.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.010
GA artistic.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.220
Oh, I understand that.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.970
I completely understand 
that, Namiko-san.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:33.740
For example?

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.070
Like culinary cubism...

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.510
Or surrealism.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:41.530
Hey, we have a practical 
cooking class, right?

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:43.280
I wanna know what we're going to make!

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.180
Kisaragi, you don't like eggs?

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:47.770
But you ordered the Tsukimi Udon...

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:51.390
Oh, I always save the egg for last.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.460
I don't like to mix it with the soup.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.490
Then you should've 
gone with plain Udon...

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:56.380
It's cheaper.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:58.990
Oh, no. This is my favorite part.

00:16:59.550 --> 00:16:59.960
<b> Sliiiiiide</b>

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:02.640
Kisaragi, you're a snake.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:03.300
Yes.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:05.840
Huh?

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.120
What could this be?

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:08.740
A bolt?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.740
Probably mine.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.210
Oh, so it was yours.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:15.200
Were you making something?

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.330
Like a production?

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.430
No. I thought I had removed them all,

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.250
but it seems like there were 
still some attached to my head.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.990
What? Kyouju-san?

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:30.840
GA! So cool!

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:32.300
Something like this?

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:33.770
Wow, amazing.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.490
Enough wood panels for the class.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.700
Looks like it.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.490
We don't need the box they 
came in anymore, right?

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:40.410
Should we crush it?

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.660
Should I just smash it?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:46.150
But don't you just want to 
climb into boxes that big?

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:47.680
Hmm... really?

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.600
Ever since I was a kid,

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:52.230
I've always loved the 
insides of cardboard boxes!

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:55.230
Ahh, Kisaragi, you really 
are like a small animal.

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:56.050
What is that?

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:57.560
Hey!

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:58.770
Oh, there was another one.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.420
<b> Ta-da!</b>

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.830
It's finally complete!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:03.790
GA original pencils!

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:05.180
What are these?

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.390
Did you make these, Noda?

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.560
Whoa, awesome!
 Lemme see!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:15.610
<b> Hubbub</b>

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.010
I printed them out and 
stuck them to the pencils.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.070
They're too nice to use!

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.610
Oh, let me see them for a second.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.880
I feel like mine's a bit 
thicker than the rest...

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.910
Oh, that's because I accidentally 
printed Namiko-san's

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:26.200
on thick paper instead.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.430
It wasn't easy wrapping 
it around the pencil!

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:30.150
It better not be on purpose.

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:34.880
Now that you mention it, 
there are people who say

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.800
they dream in black and white 
and people who dream in color.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.210
They say it has to do 
with the amount of color

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:44.320
that a person perceives 
on a daily basis.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.340
Wow.

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:47.130
For example, apparently, 
people who think a lot

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:50.000
about how they dress 
tend to dream in color.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:51.810
Wow. I dream in color.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.910
Hmm, I'm black and white.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.900
Hmm, which one am I again?

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:56.970
Kyouju, which are you?

00:18:56.970 --> 00:19:01.350
Hmm? Last night I dreamt in 
sepia tone with subtitles.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:04.450
 Fight!
Martian Robot

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:02.170
How stylish!

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:02.980
As expected.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.210
You call that "stylish"?

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:07.030
We have sketching next!

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:08.060
Sketching!

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.380
All right. Then all we need are pencils.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.730
Actually, today is charcoal sketching.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:13.200
What?

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:18.270
Um, Tomokane-san, 
where's your charcoal?

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:21.330
No! Tuesdays are crayon for me!

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:22.130
Right?

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:21.710
<b> Right?!</b>

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:23.710
Hey, hey. Don't be stubborn.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:25.440
If you forgot, 
then I'll lend you mine.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:30.170
Whenever we're sketching I 
always remember the same thing.

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:31.660
Yeah! Same here.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:32.640
“Scratch cats," right?

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.470
From Tomokane said it wrong before, right?

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.770
She sounded so confident, too!

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:37.640
Right, right!

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.010
What! You guys sure remember 
that kind of stuff well.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:40.820
Is that right?

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.790
Because since then,

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.040
Kisaragi-chan always 
looks strangely happy

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.150
whenever she's doodling.

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.260
Only during sketch class break time.

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:53.160
She's probably getting close to a

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:55.350
thousand scratch cats in her sketchbook.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.020
<b> Oh!</b>

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:10.520
<b> 5 More Minutes Later</b>

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:12.920
You were hiding in here?

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.650
Think about those of us who 
have to come looking for you!

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.860
It can just be when they 
assign art homework,

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:25.770
but I wish I could teleport!

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:29.600
Taking home all the art 
supplies is a lot of work.

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:33.230
And then bringing them all back to school!

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:41.140
Namiko-san! What should we do 
with this escaped happiness?!

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.290
Why don't you wrap it in 
a tissue and take it with you?

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:51.060
Ooh! This water-based 
marker color is new!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.820
Maybe I'll buy it!

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:56.860
Hmm. It's about time I got 
a new sketchbook, as well.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.200
Oh! There's stuff on sale over there.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:00.810
Really? Where? 
Where are they?

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.490
I'll take this 50cm ruler and...

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.940
The bus is coming,
 so I'm heading home.

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:10.470
Then I will too.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:11.560
Tomokane, what about you?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:16.920
...and maybe this masking sheet...

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:20.820
But I'm not sure if I'll 
actually end up using it, so...

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:24.260
But if I have it then I might be 
more likely to use it, so...

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.600
And it's half off...

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:26.540
But...

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.740
It doesn't look like Miss Princess 
will be done shopping anytime soon...

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:31.620
Good luck, Lord Belmont.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:34.660
What? Did the bus leave already?

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:35.910
Looks like it.

00:21:35.910 --> 00:21:38.830
Would you two mind 
hanging out for a bit?

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.790
Hmm? Sure!

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:41.510
Where to?

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.000
A stand-and-eat soba 
place in the station.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.310
I heard that it's famous for 
being pretty good around here.

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:49.020
I'm a little amazed that 
you'd suggest it, Masa.

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:50.920
When you were talking 
about Tsukimi-Udon...

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:52.760
Ooh! I kinda want to try that, too.

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:53.870
Try that?

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:40.900
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:27.020
A long, long time ago,

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.100
in a very beautiful world...

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:30.610
Oh! Are we doing a fairy tale?!

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:31.300
Are we?!

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:33.220
Huh? Where did Kisaragi go?

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:35.870
It seems as though she's been 
taken by some GA third years.

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:37.730
We're going to the supply shop too!

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:40.900
A Happy Ending

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:39.380
Oh! She's back.
